1
00:00:18,002 --> 00:00:21,318
Have you got everything? I've got
everything. Don't worry. Be careful.

2
00:00:21,358 --> 00:00:24,104
You'll have to call Mo about. . .
Oh, never mind Mo.

3
00:00:29,149 --> 00:00:32,504
OK, I'm going now. I love you.
I love you. Love you.

4
00:00:37,422 --> 00:00:39,470
I love you. Bye.

5
00:01:00,749 --> 00:01:05,742
So where are we going?
Further than we've ever gone before.

6
00:01:49,135 --> 00:01:51,893
It's the year 5,000,000,023.

7
00:01:51,933 --> 00:01:56,842
We're in the Galaxy M87
and this. . . this is New Earth.

8
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:00,219
It's just. . .

9
00:02:02,359 --> 00:02:03,758
That's just. . .

10
00:02:04,557 --> 00:02:06,710
Not bad. Not bad at all.

11
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:09,590
That's amazing.

12
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:12,067
I'll never get used to this, never.

13
00:02:12,107 --> 00:02:14,184
Different ground beneath my feet,

14
00:02:14,224 --> 00:02:15,740
different sky.

15
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,264
What's that smell?

16
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:21,296
Apple grass. Apple grass. Yeah.

17
00:02:21,336 --> 00:02:23,972
It's beautiful.

18
00:02:24,012 --> 00:02:25,649
Oh, I love this.

19
00:02:25,689 --> 00:02:27,807
Can I just say?

20
00:02:27,847 --> 00:02:30,807
Travelling with you, I love it!

21
00:02:30,847 --> 00:02:32,364
Me too!

22
00:02:33,206 --> 00:02:34,241
Come on.

23
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:40,760
Human! She's pure-blood human.

24
00:02:42,828 --> 00:02:45,126
Closer, closer.

25
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:55,973
So, the year 5,000,000,000, the Sun
expands, the Earth gets roasted.

26
00:02:56,013 --> 00:02:59,009
That was our first date.
We had chips.

27
00:03:00,688 --> 00:03:05,124
So anyway, planet gone, all rocks
and dust, but the human race lives
on, spread out across the stars.

28
00:03:05,164 --> 00:03:11,876
As soon as the Earth burns up, oh,
they get all nostalgic, big revival
movement. They find this place,

29
00:03:11,916 --> 00:03:14,354
same size as the Earth, same air,
same orbit, lovely.

30
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:17,751
The call goes out, the humans
move in. What's the city called?

31
00:03:17,791 --> 00:03:19,825
New New York. Oh, come on. It is!

32
00:03:19,865 --> 00:03:26,497
The City of New New York.
Strictly speaking, it's the 15th
New York since the original, so that

33
00:03:26,537 --> 00:03:31,696
makes it New New New New New New New
New New New New New New New York.

34
00:03:33,411 --> 00:03:35,834
What? You're so different.
New new Doctor.

35
00:03:39,005 --> 00:03:41,801
Impossible. I recognise that child.

36
00:03:41,841 --> 00:03:43,997
Her face, show me her face.

37
00:03:44,037 --> 00:03:48,582
Closer, closer. Face, face, face.

38
00:03:49,556 --> 00:03:53,348
Can we go and visit New New York -
so good they named it twice?

39
00:03:53,388 --> 00:03:57,023
Well, I thought we might go there
first.

40
00:03:57,063 --> 00:03:59,618
Why, what is it?
Some sort of hospital.

41
00:03:59,658 --> 00:04:03,572
The green moon on the side, that's
the universal symbol for hospitals.

42
00:04:03,612 --> 00:04:05,212
I got this. . .

43
00:04:05,252 --> 00:04:07,568
a message on the psychic paper.

44
00:04:07,608 --> 00:04:09,168
Someone wants to see me.

45
00:04:09,208 --> 00:04:16,041
Oh, and I thought we were just
sightseeing. Come on, then.
Let's go and buy some grapes.

46
00:04:16,081 --> 00:04:19,394
Oh! Rose Tyler, I knew it!

47
00:04:19,434 --> 00:04:24,551
That dirty blonde assassin.
She's coming here, mistress.
But this is beyond coincidence.

48
00:04:24,591 --> 00:04:28,229
This is destiny. At last,
I can be revenged on that little. . .

49
00:04:28,269 --> 00:04:31,462
Bit rich, coming from you.
I can't help it, I don't like
hospitals. They give me the creeps.

50
00:04:31,502 --> 00:04:34,416
ON PA: The pleasure gardens
will now take visitors

51
00:04:34,456 --> 00:04:38,691
carrying green or blue
identification
cards for the next 15 minutes.

52
00:04:38,731 --> 00:04:42,926
Visitors are reminded
that cuttings from the gardens
are not permitted.

53
00:04:42,966 --> 00:04:44,886
Very smart.

54
00:04:44,926 --> 00:04:48,400
Not exactly NHS.
No shop. I like the little shop.

55
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:53,235
I thought this far in the future,
they'd have cured everything.
The human race moves on - so do viruses.

56
00:04:53,275 --> 00:04:55,873
It's an ongoing war.

57
00:04:55,913 --> 00:04:57,397
Hope, harmony and health.

58
00:04:59,709 --> 00:05:05,183
They're cats. Now, don't stare.
Think what you look like to them -
all pink and yellow.

59
00:05:05,223 --> 00:05:08,333
That's where I'd put the shop,
right there.

60
00:05:10,453 --> 00:05:12,493
Ward 26, thanks.

61
00:05:12,533 --> 00:05:14,729
Override controls.

62
00:05:14,769 --> 00:05:16,088
Hold on, hold on.

63
00:05:16,128 --> 00:05:19,406
Can't, too late. I'm going up.
It's OK, there's another lift.

64
00:05:19,446 --> 00:05:22,363
Ward 26,
and watch out for the disinfectant.

65
00:05:22,403 --> 00:05:25,079
Watch out for what? The disinfectant!
The what?

66
00:05:25,119 --> 00:05:26,603
The dis. . . Oh, you'll find out.

67
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:36,254
Um. . .ward 26, thanks.

68
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:44,617
'Commence stage one disinfection.'

69
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:50,516
'Commence stage one disinfection.'

70
00:06:22,850 --> 00:06:24,566
The human child is clean.

71
00:06:24,606 --> 00:06:28,124
Um, I'm looking for ward 26.

72
00:06:28,164 --> 00:06:29,967
This way, Rose Tyler.

73
00:06:46,701 --> 00:06:49,898
Nice place. No shop downstairs -
I'd have a shop.

74
00:06:49,938 --> 00:06:53,254
Not a big one, just a shop.
So people can shop.

75
00:06:53,294 --> 00:06:57,372
The hospital is a place of healing.
A shop does some people
the world of good.

76
00:06:57,412 --> 00:06:59,669
Not me, other people.

77
00:07:01,127 --> 00:07:05,871
The Sisters of Plenitude take
a lifelong vow to help and to mend.

78
00:07:07,634 --> 00:07:09,671
Excuse me!

79
00:07:09,711 --> 00:07:14,948
Members of the public may only gaze
upon the Duke of Manhattan
with written permission

80
00:07:14,988 --> 00:07:19,062
from the Senate of New New York.
That's petrifold regression, right?
I'm dying, sir,

81
00:07:19,102 --> 00:07:22,578
a lifetime of charity and abstinence

82
00:07:22,618 --> 00:07:26,095
and it ends like this. Any statement
made by the Duke of Manhattan

83
00:07:26,135 --> 00:07:29,371
may not be made public without
official clearance. Frau Clovis!

84
00:07:31,689 --> 00:07:36,318
I'm so weak. Sister Jatt,
a little privacy, please.

85
00:07:38,278 --> 00:07:43,352
. .He'll be up and about in no time.
I doubt it. Petrifold regression -
he's turning to stone.

86
00:07:43,392 --> 00:07:47,709
There won't be a cure for, oh,
a thousand years. He might be up
and about but only as a statue.

87
00:07:47,749 --> 00:07:51,662
Have faith in the Sisterhood.
But is there no-one
here you recognise?

88
00:07:51,702 --> 00:07:55,658
It's rather unusual, to visit
without knowing the patient.

89
00:07:55,698 --> 00:07:58,001
No, I think I've found him.

90
00:08:00,975 --> 00:08:03,852
Novice Hame, if I can leave
this gentleman in your care.

91
00:08:03,892 --> 00:08:07,644
Oh, I think my friend got lost. Rose
Tyler - could you ask at reception?

92
00:08:07,684 --> 00:08:09,168
Certainly, sir.

93
00:08:11,402 --> 00:08:13,199
I'm afraid the Face of Boe's asleep.

94
00:08:13,239 --> 00:08:17,351
That's all he tends to do
these days. Are you a friend?

95
00:08:17,391 --> 00:08:20,830
We met just the once on
Platform One. What's wrong with him?

96
00:08:20,870 --> 00:08:24,503
I'm so sorry, I thought you knew.

97
00:08:24,543 --> 00:08:27,102
The Face of Boe is dying.

98
00:08:27,142 --> 00:08:30,218
Of what? Old age,

99
00:08:30,258 --> 00:08:32,136
the one thing we can't cure.

100
00:08:32,176 --> 00:08:38,888
He's thousands of years old,
some people say millions,
although that's impossible.

101
00:08:38,928 --> 00:08:41,630
Oh, I don't know. I like impossible.

102
00:08:44,082 --> 00:08:49,577
I'm here. I look a bit different,
but it's me, it's the Doctor.

103
00:09:21,717 --> 00:09:24,198
Well, you never know what your life
is going to be like, ever!

104
00:09:24,238 --> 00:09:26,032
I'm bored with this drink.

105
00:09:26,072 --> 00:09:28,750
Anyway. . . Oh, hello, darling! Oh!

106
00:09:28,790 --> 00:09:32,584
Don't, now stop it!
Wait a minute, that's. . .

107
00:09:32,624 --> 00:09:34,500
Peekaboo!

108
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:36,300
Don't you come anywhere
near me, Cassandra.

109
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:39,337
Why, what do you think
I'm going to do? Flap you to death?

110
00:09:39,377 --> 00:09:41,094
Yeah, but what about Gollum?

111
00:09:41,134 --> 00:09:43,770
Oh, that's just Chip, he's my pet.

112
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:45,370
I worship the mistress.

113
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:47,338
Moisturise me, moisturise me!

114
00:09:48,845 --> 00:09:52,004
He's not even a proper life form,
he's a force-grown clone.

115
00:09:52,044 --> 00:09:56,916
I modelled him on my favourite
pattern. But he's so faithful.

116
00:09:56,956 --> 00:09:58,794
Chip sees to my physical needs.

117
00:09:58,834 --> 00:10:00,751
I hope that means food.

118
00:10:00,791 --> 00:10:05,266
But how comes you're still alive?
After you murdered me?
That was your own fault.

119
00:10:05,306 --> 00:10:11,657
The brain of my mistress survived,
and her pretty blue eyes
were salvaged from the bin.

120
00:10:11,697 --> 00:10:14,454
But what about the skin? I saw it,

121
00:10:14,494 --> 00:10:16,412
you got ripped apart.

122
00:10:16,452 --> 00:10:19,251
That piece of skin was taken
from the front of my body.

123
00:10:19,291 --> 00:10:21,048
This piece is the back.

124
00:10:21,088 --> 00:10:25,641
Right, so you're talking out of your...
Ask not!  The mistress was lucky to survive.

125
00:10:25,681 --> 00:10:28,318
Chip secreted my lady
into the hospital.

126
00:10:28,358 --> 00:10:31,924
So they don't know you're here?
Chip steals medicine, helps my lady,

127
00:10:32,874 --> 00:10:35,591
soothes her, strokes her.

128
00:10:35,631 --> 00:10:42,265
You can stop right there, Chip.
But I'm so alone, hidden down here,
the last human in existence.

129
00:10:42,305 --> 00:10:44,938
Don't start that!
They've called this planet New Earth.

130
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:50,932
A vegetable patch. And there's
millions of humans out there,
millions of them. Mutant stock.

131
00:10:50,972 --> 00:10:54,885
They evolved, Cassandra,
they just evolved, like they should.

132
00:10:54,925 --> 00:11:00,240
You stayed still, you got yourself
all pickled and preserved,
and what good did it do you?

133
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:03,595
I remember that night, drinks
for the Ambassador of Thrace.

134
00:11:03,635 --> 00:11:05,235
'. .How very kind you are. . .'

135
00:11:05,275 --> 00:11:08,671
That was the last time
anyone told me I was beautiful.

136
00:11:08,711 --> 00:11:12,308
After that,
it all became such hard work.

137
00:11:12,348 --> 00:11:15,186
Well, you've got a knack
for survival, I'll give you that.

138
00:11:15,226 --> 00:11:20,419
But I've not been idle, Rose.
Tucked away underneath
this hospital, I've been listening.

139
00:11:20,459 --> 00:11:22,773
The Sisters are hiding something.

140
00:11:22,813 --> 00:11:26,769
What do you mean?
Oh, these cats have secrets.

141
00:11:26,809 --> 00:11:30,085
Hush, let me whisper. Come close.

142
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:33,362
You must be joking if you think
I'm coming anywhere near you.

143
00:11:33,402 --> 00:11:37,435
Chip, activate the psychograft.
I can't move!

144
00:11:37,475 --> 00:11:39,164
Cassandra, let me go!

145
00:11:40,952 --> 00:11:43,389
What are you doing?
The lady's moving on.

146
00:11:43,429 --> 00:11:47,530
It's goodbye, trampoline,
and hello, blondie!

147
00:11:58,849 --> 00:12:03,478
Mistress?
CASSANDRA'S ACCENT: Moisturise me.

148
00:12:08,523 --> 00:12:11,315
How bizarre,

149
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:13,553
arms,

150
00:12:13,593 --> 00:12:15,111
fingers, hair!

151
00:12:17,589 --> 00:12:20,626
Let me see, let me see.

152
00:12:21,665 --> 00:12:24,063
Oh, my God.

153
00:12:24,103 --> 00:12:26,179
I'm a chav!

154
00:12:26,219 --> 00:12:28,977
Hope, harmony and health.

155
00:12:29,017 --> 00:12:31,813
Hope, harmony and health.

156
00:12:31,853 --> 00:12:35,086
That's very kind, there's no need.

157
00:12:35,126 --> 00:12:36,764
You're the one working.

158
00:12:36,804 --> 00:12:39,964
There's not much to do,
just maintain his smoke.

159
00:12:40,004 --> 00:12:44,836
And I suppose I'm company.
I can hear him singing sometimes,

160
00:12:44,876 --> 00:12:47,073
in my mind,

161
00:12:47,113 --> 00:12:50,991
such ancient songs.
Am I the only visitor?

162
00:12:51,031 --> 00:12:54,504
The rest of Boekind became extinct,
long ago.

163
00:12:54,544 --> 00:12:56,264
He's the only one left.

164
00:12:56,304 --> 00:13:00,420
Legend says that the Face of Boe
has watched the universe grow old.

165
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:04,933
There's all sorts of superstitions
around him.

166
00:13:04,973 --> 00:13:08,495
One story
says that just before his death,

167
00:13:08,535 --> 00:13:11,483
the Face of Boe will impart
his great secret,

168
00:13:11,523 --> 00:13:15,958
that he will speak those words
only to one like himself.

169
00:13:15,998 --> 00:13:18,917
What does that mean?
It's just a story.

170
00:13:18,957 --> 00:13:23,110
Tell me the rest.
It's said he'll talk to a wanderer,

171
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:25,388
to the man without a home,

172
00:13:25,428 --> 00:13:26,911
the lonely god.

173
00:13:32,461 --> 00:13:36,534
Look at me! From class to brass.

174
00:13:36,574 --> 00:13:38,456
Although. . .

175
00:13:38,496 --> 00:13:41,772
Ooh. . .curves.

176
00:13:41,812 --> 00:13:43,568
Oh, baby!

177
00:13:43,608 --> 00:13:47,324
It's like living inside a bouncy
castle. The mistress is beautiful.

178
00:13:47,364 --> 00:13:48,878
Absolument.

179
00:13:48,918 --> 00:13:50,607
Oh, but look.

180
00:13:53,474 --> 00:13:56,111
The brain meat expired.

181
00:13:56,151 --> 00:13:57,908
My old mistress has gone.

182
00:13:57,948 --> 00:14:01,227
But safe and sound in here.

183
00:14:01,267 --> 00:14:03,784
But what of the Rose child's mind?

184
00:14:03,824 --> 00:14:05,701
Oh, tucked away.

185
00:14:05,741 --> 00:14:08,204
I can just about access
the surface memory, she's. . .

186
00:14:10,695 --> 00:14:13,357
Gosh, she's with the Doctor.

187
00:14:14,932 --> 00:14:17,129
That man,

188
00:14:17,169 --> 00:14:22,361
he's the Doctor, the same Doctor,
with a new face.

189
00:14:22,401 --> 00:14:26,476
That hypocrite. . . ! Though I must get
the name of his surgeon.

190
00:14:26,516 --> 00:14:28,395
I could do with a little work.

191
00:14:28,435 --> 00:14:29,953
Although. . .

192
00:14:31,708 --> 00:14:34,256
Nice rear bumper.

193
00:14:36,345 --> 00:14:38,781
MOBILE RINGS
Oh, it seems to be ringing.

194
00:14:38,821 --> 00:14:40,539
Is it meant to ring?

195
00:14:40,579 --> 00:14:44,655
A primitive communications device.
DOCTOR: Rose? Where are you?

196
00:14:44,695 --> 00:14:46,532
How does she speak?

197
00:14:46,572 --> 00:14:48,750
Old Earth cockney. Um. . .

198
00:14:50,289 --> 00:14:53,325
Wotcha. Where've you been? How long
does it take to get to ward 26?

199
00:14:53,365 --> 00:14:55,242
I'm on my way, guvnor.

200
00:14:55,282 --> 00:14:59,798
I shall proceed
up the apples and pears.

201
00:14:59,838 --> 00:15:03,629
You'll never guess, I'm with
the Face of Boe. Remember him?

202
00:15:03,669 --> 00:15:07,705
Of course I do. That big old. . .

203
00:15:07,745 --> 00:15:10,703
boat race.
Better go. See you in a minute.

204
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:14,179
DUKE OF MANHATTAN LAUGHS
Didn't think I was going to make it!

205
00:15:14,219 --> 00:15:19,452
It's that man again. He's my good
luck charm. Come in, don't be shy.

206
00:15:19,492 --> 00:15:24,689
Any friendship expressed
by the Duke of Manhattan does not
constitute a form of legal contract.

207
00:15:24,729 --> 00:15:26,611
Winch me up.

208
00:15:27,564 --> 00:15:33,079
Hup! Look at me.
No sign of infection. Champagne, sir?

209
00:15:33,119 --> 00:15:34,916
No, thanks.

210
00:15:34,956 --> 00:15:41,673
You had petrifold regression, right?
Had being the operative word,
past tense! Completely cured.

211
00:15:43,185 --> 00:15:47,259
But that's impossible. Primitive
species would accuse us of magic

212
00:15:47,299 --> 00:15:50,297
but it's merely
the tender application of science.

213
00:15:50,337 --> 00:15:53,733
How on earth did you cure him?
How on New Earth, you might say.

214
00:15:53,773 --> 00:15:56,730
What's in that solution?
A simple remedy.

215
00:15:56,770 --> 00:15:58,370
Then tell me what it is.

216
00:15:58,410 --> 00:16:01,206
I'm sorry - patient confidentiality.

217
00:16:01,246 --> 00:16:03,242
I don't believe we've met.

218
00:16:03,282 --> 00:16:04,999
My name is Matron Casp.

219
00:16:05,039 --> 00:16:06,518
I'm The Doctor.

220
00:16:06,558 --> 00:16:08,677
I think you will find that
WE'RE the doctors here.

221
00:16:08,717 --> 00:16:12,487
Matron Casp, you're needed in
intensive care. If you'd excuse me.

222
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:17,904
It's happened again,
one of the patients is conscious.

223
00:16:17,944 --> 00:16:19,996
Well, we can't have that.

224
00:16:21,219 --> 00:16:26,414
This Doctor man is dangerous.
Dangerous and clever.
I might need a mind like his.

225
00:16:26,454 --> 00:16:28,210
The Sisterhood is up to something.

226
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:32,366
Remember that Old Earth saying,
never trust a nun,

227
00:16:32,406 --> 00:16:36,323
never trust a nurse,
and never trust a cat.

228
00:16:36,363 --> 00:16:38,132
Perfume?

229
00:16:42,518 --> 00:16:49,514
It was having a perfectly normal
blood-wash, then all of a sudden,
it started crying. It's this one.

230
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:55,177
Please. . .help me.
Look at its eyes, so alive.

231
00:16:55,217 --> 00:16:56,777
Positively sparkling.

232
00:16:56,817 --> 00:16:59,173
Please, where am I?

233
00:16:59,213 --> 00:17:00,812
And speech!

234
00:17:00,852 --> 00:17:02,851
How can it even have a vocabulary?

235
00:17:02,891 --> 00:17:08,605
Sister Corvin has written a thesis
on the migration of sentience,
she calls it the echo of life.

236
00:17:08,645 --> 00:17:10,365
It's well worth a read.

237
00:17:10,405 --> 00:17:12,081
Help me.

238
00:17:12,121 --> 00:17:13,594
I've seen enough, thank you.

239
00:17:14,998 --> 00:17:18,872
If this happens again, we might
have to review our brainstem policy.

240
00:17:18,912 --> 00:17:20,512
And what should we do
with the patient?

241
00:17:20,552 --> 00:17:22,032
Standard procedure.

242
00:17:22,072 --> 00:17:23,272
Incinerate.

243
00:17:25,665 --> 00:17:27,713
SCREAMS

244
00:17:33,414 --> 00:17:39,365
'Ambient temperature is 14 degrees
composite, a temperature designed
to promote healing and well-being.'

245
00:17:39,405 --> 00:17:43,245
There you are!
Come and look at this patient.

246
00:17:43,285 --> 00:17:45,841
Marconi's disease,
should take years to recover.

247
00:17:45,881 --> 00:17:48,238
Two days.
I've never seen anything like it.

248
00:17:48,278 --> 00:17:50,755
They've invented a cell-washing
cascade, it's amazing.

249
00:17:50,795 --> 00:17:53,751
Their medical science
is way advanced.

250
00:17:53,791 --> 00:17:58,586
And this one, pallidome pancrosis.
Kills you in ten minutes -
and he's fine.

251
00:18:00,265 --> 00:18:02,541
I need to find a terminal. Gotta see
how they do this.

252
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:06,772
If they've got the best medicine in
the world, why's it such a secret?

253
00:18:06,812 --> 00:18:08,932
I can't Adam and Eve it.

254
00:18:08,972 --> 00:18:11,528
What. . . ? What's with the voice?

255
00:18:11,568 --> 00:18:14,565
I don't know, just larking about.

256
00:18:14,605 --> 00:18:17,432
New Earth. . .new me.

257
00:18:19,319 --> 00:18:21,479
Well, I can talk - new new Doctor.

258
00:18:21,519 --> 00:18:23,811
Mmm, aren't you just?

259
00:18:32,946 --> 00:18:34,868
T-Terminal's this way.

260
00:18:39,899 --> 00:18:41,415
FALSETTO: Yup,

261
00:18:41,455 --> 00:18:42,575
still got it.

262
00:18:42,615 --> 00:18:47,885
Nope, nothing odd.
Surgery, post-op, nanodentistry.

263
00:18:47,925 --> 00:18:51,760
No sign of a shop,
they should have a shop.
No, it's missing something else.

264
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:57,275
When I was downstairs, those
nurse cat nuns were talking about
intensive care, but where is it?

265
00:18:57,315 --> 00:18:58,872
You're right, well done.

266
00:18:58,912 --> 00:19:02,230
Why would they
hide a whole department?

267
00:19:02,270 --> 00:19:04,986
It's got to be there somewhere,
search the subframe.

268
00:19:05,026 --> 00:19:07,103
What if the subframe's locked?

269
00:19:07,143 --> 00:19:09,224
Try the installation protocol.

270
00:19:09,264 --> 00:19:11,726
Yeah, course, sorry. Hold on.

271
00:19:23,286 --> 00:19:26,200
Intensive care. . .

272
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:28,497
Certainly looks intensive.

273
00:20:09,430 --> 00:20:10,950
That's disgusting.

274
00:20:10,990 --> 00:20:13,904
What's wrong with him?

275
00:20:13,944 --> 00:20:16,581
I'm sorry.

276
00:20:16,621 --> 00:20:18,435
I'm so sorry.

277
00:20:34,161 --> 00:20:36,398
What disease is that?

278
00:20:36,438 --> 00:20:41,470
All of them. Every single disease
in the galaxy. They've been
infected with everything.

279
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:45,107
What about us,

280
00:20:45,147 --> 00:20:48,143
are we safe? The air's sterile.
Just don't touch them.

281
00:20:55,094 --> 00:20:57,615
How many patients are there?

282
00:20:57,655 --> 00:20:59,412
They're not patients.

283
00:20:59,452 --> 00:21:01,052
But they're sick.

284
00:21:01,092 --> 00:21:03,528
They were born sick.
They're meant to be sick.

285
00:21:03,568 --> 00:21:05,364
They exist to be sick.

286
00:21:05,404 --> 00:21:08,841
Lab rats. No wonder the Sisters
have a cure for everything,

287
00:21:08,881 --> 00:21:13,392
they've built the ultimate
research laboratory - a human farm!

288
00:21:13,432 --> 00:21:15,551
Why don't they just die?

289
00:21:15,591 --> 00:21:18,348
Plague carriers,

290
00:21:18,388 --> 00:21:21,184
the last to go.
It's for the greater cause.

291
00:21:21,224 --> 00:21:24,256
Novice Hame.

292
00:21:25,738 --> 00:21:27,536
When you took your vows,
did you agree to this?

293
00:21:27,576 --> 00:21:29,855
The Sisterhood has sworn to help.

294
00:21:29,895 --> 00:21:32,371
What, by killing?
But they're not real people.

295
00:21:32,411 --> 00:21:37,765
They're specially grown,
they have no proper existence.

296
00:21:37,805 --> 00:21:39,642
What's the turnover?

297
00:21:39,682 --> 00:21:42,442
A thousand a day? Thousand the next?

298
00:21:42,482 --> 00:21:44,439
Thousand the next?
How many thousands?

299
00:21:44,479 --> 00:21:46,915
For how many years? HOW MANY?

300
00:21:46,955 --> 00:21:51,909
Mankind needed us. They came
to this planet with so many
illnesses, we couldn't cope.

301
00:21:51,949 --> 00:21:54,626
We did try,

302
00:21:54,666 --> 00:22:01,776
we tried everything. We tried
using clone-meat and biocattle.
The results were too slow.

303
00:22:01,816 --> 00:22:05,172
So the Sisterhood grew its own flesh,

304
00:22:05,212 --> 00:22:07,769
that's all they are, flesh.

305
00:22:07,809 --> 00:22:09,406
These people are alive.

306
00:22:09,446 --> 00:22:12,446
But think of those humans out there,

307
00:22:12,486 --> 00:22:15,562
healthy and happy because of us.

308
00:22:15,602 --> 00:22:19,320
If they live because of this,
then life is worthless.

309
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:22,156
But who are you to decide that?

310
00:22:22,196 --> 00:22:24,072
I'm the Doctor.

311
00:22:24,112 --> 00:22:27,306
And if you don't like it,
if you want to take it to a higher
authority, there isn't one.

312
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:29,942
It stops with me.

313
00:22:29,982 --> 00:22:34,896
Just to confirm,
none of the humans in the city
actually know about this?

314
00:22:34,936 --> 00:22:38,373
We thought it best not. Hold on.
I can understand the bodies.

315
00:22:38,413 --> 00:22:41,570
I can understand your vows,
but one thing I can't understand.

316
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:45,884
What have you done to Rose?
I don't know what you mean.
And I'm being very, very calm -

317
00:22:45,924 --> 00:22:48,203
you want to beware of that -
very, very calm.

318
00:22:48,243 --> 00:22:52,517
And the only reason I'm being
so very, very calm is that
the brain is a delicate thing.

319
00:22:52,557 --> 00:22:57,553
Whatever you've done to Rose's head,
I want it reversed.
We haven't done anything.

320
00:22:57,593 --> 00:22:59,429
I'm perfectly fine.

321
00:22:59,469 --> 00:23:03,266
These people are dying.
And Rose would care.

322
00:23:03,306 --> 00:23:06,259
Oh, all right, cleverclogs. . .

323
00:23:06,299 --> 00:23:08,307
smartypants. . .

324
00:23:10,454 --> 00:23:17,166
ladykiller. What's happened to you?
I knew something was going on in
this hospital but I needed this body

325
00:23:17,206 --> 00:23:20,124
and your mind to find it out.

326
00:23:20,164 --> 00:23:25,637
Who are you? The last human.

327
00:23:25,677 --> 00:23:28,583
Cassandra?
Wake up and smell the perfume.

328
00:23:32,111 --> 00:23:34,147
You've hurt him! I don't understand.

329
00:23:34,187 --> 00:23:35,827
I'll have to fetch matron.

330
00:23:35,867 --> 00:23:40,126
You do that - cos I want to see her.
Now run along! Sound the alarm!

331
00:23:44,573 --> 00:23:47,132
Matron, it's that man and the girl.

332
00:23:47,172 --> 00:23:50,408
We heard the alarm. Now go back
to work, tend to your patients.

333
00:23:58,517 --> 00:24:00,117
Let me out! Let me out!

334
00:24:00,157 --> 00:24:03,352
Aren't you lucky there was a spare.

335
00:24:03,392 --> 00:24:06,631
Standing room only.
You've stolen Rose's body.

336
00:24:06,671 --> 00:24:11,424
Over the years, I've thought of
a thousand ways to kill you, Doctor,

337
00:24:11,464 --> 00:24:15,100
and now that's exactly what
I've got - one thousand diseases.

338
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:20,732
They pump the patients with a top-up
every ten minutes, you've got
about three minutes left.

339
00:24:20,772 --> 00:24:27,085
Enjoy. Just let Rose go, Cassandra.
I will, as soon as I find
someone younger and. . .

340
00:24:27,125 --> 00:24:32,318
less common. Then I'll junk her
with the waste.
Now, hushabye - it's showtime.

341
00:24:32,358 --> 00:24:34,835
Anything we can do to help?

342
00:24:34,875 --> 00:24:38,436
Straight to the point, Whiskers.
I want money.

343
00:24:38,476 --> 00:24:43,065
The Sisterhood is a charity,
we don't give money, we only accept.

344
00:24:43,105 --> 00:24:47,380
The humans across the water
pay you a fortune
and that's exactly what I need.

345
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:50,218
A one-off payment,
that's all I want.

346
00:24:50,258 --> 00:24:51,695
And perhaps a yacht.

347
00:24:51,735 --> 00:24:56,647
In return for which,
I will tell the city nothing
of your institutional murder.

348
00:24:56,687 --> 00:24:59,204
Is that a deal?

349
00:24:59,244 --> 00:25:03,002
I'm afraid not. I'd really
advise you to think about this.

350
00:25:03,042 --> 00:25:05,598
There's no need. I have to decline.

351
00:25:05,638 --> 00:25:07,875
I'll tell them,
and you've no way of stopping me!

352
00:25:07,915 --> 00:25:11,153
You're not exactly nuns with guns.
You're not even armed.

353
00:25:11,193 --> 00:25:14,838
Who needs arms when we have claws?

354
00:25:16,506 --> 00:25:19,009
Oh, well. Nice try. . .Chip! Plan B.

355
00:25:29,293 --> 00:25:30,965
What have you done?

356
00:25:31,005 --> 00:25:33,166
Gave the system a shot
of adrenalin just to wake 'em up.

357
00:25:33,206 --> 00:25:34,882
See ya. Don't touch them!

358
00:25:34,922 --> 00:25:37,600
Whatever you do, don't touch.

359
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:39,716
Please, save us.

360
00:25:39,756 --> 00:25:41,756
Save us.

361
00:25:41,796 --> 00:25:44,153
I think we should withdraw.

362
00:25:44,193 --> 00:25:47,190
We understood what you did to us.

363
00:25:47,230 --> 00:25:49,786
As part of the machine,

364
00:25:49,826 --> 00:25:51,544
we know the machine.

365
00:25:51,584 --> 00:25:55,223
Fascinating! It's actually
constructing an argument.

366
00:25:55,263 --> 00:25:58,214
And we will end it.

367
00:26:19,590 --> 00:26:21,508
They're free!

368
00:26:21,548 --> 00:26:25,489
By the Goddess Santori,
the Flesh is free!

369
00:26:27,784 --> 00:26:30,002
You caused the pain.

370
00:26:44,082 --> 00:26:46,958
Oh, my God!
What the hell have you done?

371
00:26:46,998 --> 00:26:50,594
It wasn't me. One touch and you get
every disease in the world! And
I want that body safe, Cassandra.

372
00:26:50,634 --> 00:26:52,750
We've got to go down.
But there's thousands of them.

373
00:26:52,790 --> 00:26:55,287
Run! Down, down, go down!

374
00:26:58,783 --> 00:27:01,301
Quarantine the building!

375
00:27:01,341 --> 00:27:03,269
'This building is under quarantine.'

376
00:27:05,658 --> 00:27:09,013
'Repeat.
This building is under quarantine.

377
00:27:09,053 --> 00:27:13,008
'No-one may leave the premises.
Repeat. . .

378
00:27:13,048 --> 00:27:16,843
'No-one may leave the premises. . .'

379
00:27:16,883 --> 00:27:19,915
Keep going, going down!

380
00:27:28,031 --> 00:27:30,818
Help me! (Help us. . .)

381
00:27:45,412 --> 00:27:50,405
No, the lifts have closed down.
That's the quarantine -
nothing's moving. This way!

382
00:27:54,202 --> 00:27:57,515
Oh-h!
Someone will touch him! Leave him!

383
00:27:57,555 --> 00:28:00,431
He's a clone thing, he's only got
a half-life, come on. Mistress!

384
00:28:00,471 --> 00:28:02,789
I'm sorry, I can't let her escape.

385
00:28:02,829 --> 00:28:04,347
My mistress!

386
00:28:12,536 --> 00:28:16,266
Excuse me,
can we get some service?

387
00:28:32,995 --> 00:28:35,871
We're trapped!
What are we going to do?

388
00:28:35,911 --> 00:28:38,625
Well, for starters,
you're going to leave that body.

389
00:28:38,665 --> 00:28:41,422
That psychograft is banned
on every civilised planet.

390
00:28:41,462 --> 00:28:43,222
You're compressing Rose to death.

391
00:28:43,262 --> 00:28:46,735
But I've got nowhere to go.
My original skin's dead.

392
00:28:46,775 --> 00:28:48,494
Not my problem.

393
00:28:48,533 --> 00:28:51,576
You can float as atoms in the air.
Now get out.

394
00:28:53,610 --> 00:28:56,477
Give her back to me.
You asked for it.

395
00:29:04,156 --> 00:29:08,251
Oh, my head. Where did she go?

396
00:29:09,709 --> 00:29:11,589
Oh, my, this is. . .different.

397
00:29:11,629 --> 00:29:13,743
Cassandra?

398
00:29:13,783 --> 00:29:15,262
Goodness me, I'm a man!

399
00:29:15,302 --> 00:29:17,619
Yum. So many parts!

400
00:29:17,659 --> 00:29:19,667
And hardly used.

401
00:29:21,814 --> 00:29:23,492
Ah-h. . . ! Two hearts!

402
00:29:23,532 --> 00:29:26,129
Oh, baby, I'm beating out a samba.

403
00:29:26,169 --> 00:29:28,806
Get out of him! Hmm, he's slim

404
00:29:28,846 --> 00:29:30,603
and a little bit foxy.

405
00:29:30,643 --> 00:29:32,762
You thought so too,

406
00:29:32,802 --> 00:29:34,799
I've been inside your head.

407
00:29:34,839 --> 00:29:37,557
You've been looking.

408
00:29:37,597 --> 00:29:39,479
You like it.

409
00:29:40,593 --> 00:29:44,110
What do we do? What would he do?
The Doctor,
what the hell would he do?

410
00:29:44,150 --> 00:29:46,307
Ladder, we've got to get up.

411
00:29:46,347 --> 00:29:48,386
Out of the way, blondie.

412
00:29:48,426 --> 00:29:53,254
(Help us. Please. . .help us.)

413
00:30:16,589 --> 00:30:21,827
If you get out of the Doctor's
body, he can think of something.
Oh, "Yap yap yap" (!)

414
00:30:21,867 --> 00:30:25,263
God, it was tedious
inside your head - Hormone City(!)

415
00:30:25,303 --> 00:30:27,176
We'll die if. . .

416
00:30:27,216 --> 00:30:30,094
GET OFF!

417
00:30:30,134 --> 00:30:37,168
All our good work, all that healing,
the good name of the Sisterhood -
you have destroyed everything.

418
00:30:37,208 --> 00:30:40,560
Go and play with a ball of string.
Everywhere - disease.

419
00:30:40,600 --> 00:30:43,558
This is the human world - sickness.

420
00:30:43,598 --> 00:30:45,776
SHE YOWLS

421
00:30:52,110 --> 00:30:53,668
THUD ECHOES

422
00:30:55,944 --> 00:30:57,901
Move!

423
00:30:57,941 --> 00:31:00,061
ON PA: Maximum quarantine

424
00:31:00,101 --> 00:31:01,949
Divert all shuttles.

425
00:31:03,651 --> 00:31:04,731
(Help us.)

426
00:31:04,771 --> 00:31:10,964
Now what do we do? Use the sonic
screwdriver. You mean this thing?
Yes, I mean that thing!

427
00:31:11,004 --> 00:31:13,842
But I don't know how, that Doctor's
hidden away all his thoughts.

428
00:31:13,882 --> 00:31:18,801
Cassandra, go back into me.
The Doctor can open it. Do it!
Hold on tight.

429
00:31:23,950 --> 00:31:26,987
Oh, chavtastic again(!)

430
00:31:27,027 --> 00:31:29,945
Open it! Not till you get out
of her. We need the Doctor.

431
00:31:29,985 --> 00:31:31,458
I order you to leave her!

432
00:31:34,378 --> 00:31:38,416
No matter how difficult
the situation,
there is no need to shout.

433
00:31:38,456 --> 00:31:40,568
Cassandra, get out of him!

434
00:31:40,608 --> 00:31:44,628
But if I go into you, he
simply refuses. He's so rude.
I don't care, just do something!

435
00:31:45,766 --> 00:31:47,654
I'm so going to regret this.

436
00:31:51,755 --> 00:31:55,472
Oh, sweet Lord(!) I look disgusting.

437
00:31:55,512 --> 00:31:57,631
Nice to have you back.

438
00:31:57,671 --> 00:31:59,074
No you don't!

439
00:32:01,945 --> 00:32:04,383
That was your last
warning, Cassandra.

440
00:32:04,423 --> 00:32:06,317
Inside her head. . .

441
00:32:08,018 --> 00:32:09,896
They're so alone.

442
00:32:09,936 --> 00:32:13,753
They keep reaching out
just to hold us.

443
00:32:14,692 --> 00:32:18,787
All their lives,
and they've never been touched.

444
00:32:29,833 --> 00:32:32,131
BANGING ON DOOR

445
00:32:38,863 --> 00:32:40,900
We're safe, we're safe, we're safe!

446
00:32:40,940 --> 00:32:43,336
We're clean, we're clean!
Look, look. Show me your skin.

447
00:32:43,376 --> 00:32:50,528
Look, clean. Look. If we'd been
touched, we'd be dead. So how's it
going up here, what's the status?

448
00:32:50,568 --> 00:32:55,639
Silence from the other wards. I think
we're the only ones left. I've been
trying to override the quarantine.

449
00:32:55,679 --> 00:33:00,076
If I can trip a signal
over to New New York, they can send
a private executive squad. You can't.

450
00:33:00,116 --> 00:33:04,990
If they forced entry, they'd break
quarantine. I'm not dying here! We
can't let a particle of disease out.

451
00:33:05,030 --> 00:33:10,223
There's 10 million people in that
city. They'd all be at risk. Now
turn it off! Not if it gets me out.

452
00:33:10,263 --> 00:33:16,976
OK, fine. I have to stop you lot as
well. Suits me. Rose, Novice Hame,
everyone! . .Excuse me, your Grace.

453
00:33:17,016 --> 00:33:20,457
Get me the intravenous solutions
for every single disease. Move it!

454
00:33:34,433 --> 00:33:37,830
How's that? Will that do?
I don't know! Will it do for what?

455
00:33:37,870 --> 00:33:41,987
The lifts aren't working.
Not MOVING. Different thing.

456
00:33:42,027 --> 00:33:46,083
Here we go.
But you're not going to. . .

457
00:33:48,221 --> 00:33:50,057
What do you think you're doing?

458
00:33:50,097 --> 00:33:51,489
MUFFLED: Going down!

459
00:33:54,654 --> 00:33:56,294
Come on.

460
00:33:56,334 --> 00:33:58,208
Not in a million years.

461
00:33:58,248 --> 00:34:03,524
I need another pair of hands.
What do you think? If you're
so desperate to stay alive,

462
00:34:03,564 --> 00:34:04,968
why don't you live a little?

463
00:34:05,844 --> 00:34:07,358
Seal the door!

464
00:34:07,398 --> 00:34:10,350
(Help. . . ! Please. . . !)

465
00:34:13,707 --> 00:34:15,425
You're completely mad.

466
00:34:15,465 --> 00:34:18,704
I can see why she likes you.
Going down.

467
00:34:18,744 --> 00:34:21,855
DOCTOR WHOOPS
CASSANDRA SCREAMS

468
00:34:32,288 --> 00:34:33,927
Well, that's one way to lose weight.

469
00:34:33,967 --> 00:34:35,645
Now listen, when I say so
take hold of this lever.

470
00:34:35,685 --> 00:34:38,241
But there's still a
quarantine down there, we can't. . .

471
00:34:38,281 --> 00:34:40,839
HOLD THAT LEVER!
I'm cooking up a cocktail.

472
00:34:40,879 --> 00:34:43,170
I know a bit about medicine myself.

473
00:34:52,062 --> 00:34:55,538
Now that lever's gonna resist,
but keep it in position.

474
00:34:55,578 --> 00:35:00,748
Hold on to it with everything you've
got. What about you? I've got an
appointment. "The Doctor is in."

475
00:35:08,404 --> 00:35:11,601
I'm in here. Come on.
Don't TELL them! Hold that lever.

476
00:35:13,798 --> 00:35:16,955
Come and get me, come on.
I'm in here, come on.

477
00:35:16,995 --> 00:35:21,745
LIFT: Commence stage one disinfection.
Hurry up, Come on!

478
00:35:24,826 --> 00:35:26,463
Come on. Come on.

479
00:35:32,096 --> 00:35:34,692
All they want to do is pass it on.

480
00:35:34,732 --> 00:35:37,730
PASS IT ON! Pass on what?

481
00:35:37,770 --> 00:35:40,767
Pass on what? PASS IT ON!

482
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:20,600
What did they pass on?
Did you kill them? All of them?

483
00:36:20,640 --> 00:36:24,047
No, that's YOUR way of doing things.

484
00:36:25,913 --> 00:36:28,780
I'm the Doctor, and I cured them.

485
00:36:32,427 --> 00:36:35,302
That's right, h-hey!

486
00:36:35,342 --> 00:36:37,022
There we go, sweetheart.

487
00:36:37,062 --> 00:36:38,737
Eh?

488
00:36:38,777 --> 00:36:40,773
You go to him,

489
00:36:40,813 --> 00:36:43,570
go on, that's it,

490
00:36:43,610 --> 00:36:48,008
It's a new sub-species, Cassandra,
a brand new form of life.

491
00:36:48,048 --> 00:36:50,844
New humans. Look at them. Look!

492
00:36:50,884 --> 00:36:59,233
Run by cats,
kept in the dark, fed by tubes,
but completely, completely alive.

493
00:36:59,273 --> 00:37:01,530
You can't deny them,
cos you helped create them.

494
00:37:03,030 --> 00:37:06,745
The human race just keeps on going,
keeps on changing.

495
00:37:06,785 --> 00:37:08,783
Life will out!

496
00:37:08,823 --> 00:37:10,421
Ha!

497
00:37:11,420 --> 00:37:14,737
'This is the NNYPD.
Please step away from the showers.'

498
00:37:14,777 --> 00:37:18,287
'All staff will present
themselves to the officers
for immediate arrest.

499
00:37:18,327 --> 00:37:20,848
'I repeat - immediate arrest.

500
00:37:20,888 --> 00:37:24,962
'All new life-forms will be
catalogued and taken into care.

501
00:37:25,002 --> 00:37:30,754
'All visitors to the hospital
will be required to make
a statement to the NNYPD.'

502
00:37:30,794 --> 00:37:32,972
The Face of Boe!

503
00:37:43,384 --> 00:37:45,104
You were supposed to be dying.

504
00:37:45,144 --> 00:37:48,455
'There are better things to do
today. Dying can wait.'

505
00:37:48,495 --> 00:37:51,050
Oh, I hate telepathy.

506
00:37:51,090 --> 00:37:55,125
Just what I need,
a headful of big face. Shh!

507
00:37:55,165 --> 00:37:59,801
'I had grown tired with
the universe, Doctor, but you
have taught me to look at it anew.'

508
00:37:59,841 --> 00:38:02,478
There are legends, you know,

509
00:38:02,518 --> 00:38:05,275
saying that you're
millions of years old.

510
00:38:05,315 --> 00:38:08,111
That would be impossible.
Wouldn't it just(? )

511
00:38:08,151 --> 00:38:11,828
I got the impression there was
something you wanted to tell me.

512
00:38:11,868 --> 00:38:15,422
The great secret.
So the legend says.

513
00:38:15,462 --> 00:38:18,141
It can wait. Oh, does it have to?

514
00:38:18,181 --> 00:38:20,298
We shall meet again, Doctor.

515
00:38:20,338 --> 00:38:22,895
For the third time,
for the last time.

516
00:38:22,935 --> 00:38:25,092
And the truth shall be told.

517
00:38:25,132 --> 00:38:26,934
Until that day. . .

518
00:38:32,362 --> 00:38:34,557
That is enigmatic.

519
00:38:34,597 --> 00:38:36,855
That. . . That is textbook enigmatic.

520
00:38:39,516 --> 00:38:41,325
And now for you.

521
00:38:42,550 --> 00:38:44,788
But. . .everything's happy,

522
00:38:44,828 --> 00:38:48,185
everything's fine,
can't you just leave me?

523
00:38:48,225 --> 00:38:49,982
You've lived long enough.

524
00:38:50,022 --> 00:38:53,712
Leave that body and end it,
Cassandra.

525
00:38:55,138 --> 00:38:56,975
I don't want to die.

526
00:38:57,015 --> 00:38:59,332
No-one does. Help me!

527
00:38:59,372 --> 00:39:01,091
I can't. Mistress!

528
00:39:01,131 --> 00:39:03,169
You're alive!

529
00:39:03,209 --> 00:39:06,600
I kept myself safe -
for you, mistress.

530
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:08,760
A body!

531
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:12,075
And not just that, a volunteer.

532
00:39:12,115 --> 00:39:18,629
Don't you dare! He's got a life of
his own. But I worship the mistress,
I welcome her. You can't, Cassandra.

533
00:39:18,669 --> 00:39:20,108
You. . .

534
00:39:21,303 --> 00:39:22,543
All right?

535
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:25,700
Whoa!

536
00:39:25,740 --> 00:39:27,223
OK?

537
00:39:28,656 --> 00:39:29,771
Yeah.

538
00:39:31,572 --> 00:39:34,490
Hello. Hello. Welcome back.

539
00:39:34,530 --> 00:39:39,886
Oh, sweet lord, I'm a walking
doodle. You can't stay in there.
I'm sorry, Cassandra, it's not fair.

540
00:39:39,926 --> 00:39:44,835
I can take you to the city, they can
build you a skintank and you can
stand trial for what you've done.

541
00:39:44,875 --> 00:39:47,112
Well, that would be rather dramatic.

542
00:39:47,152 --> 00:39:51,430
Possibly my finest hour -
certainly my finest hat.
But I'm afraid we don't have time.

543
00:39:51,470 --> 00:39:58,340
Poor little Chip, he's only
a half-life, and he's been through
so much, his heart is racing so.

544
00:39:58,380 --> 00:40:01,251
He's failing.
I don't think he's going to last. . .

545
00:40:01,977 --> 00:40:03,456
Are you all right? I'm fine.

546
00:40:08,209 --> 00:40:11,689
I'm dying, but that's fine.

547
00:40:13,323 --> 00:40:15,361
I can take you to the city.

548
00:40:15,401 --> 00:40:17,361
No, you won't.

549
00:40:17,401 --> 00:40:19,433
Everything's new on this planet.

550
00:40:19,473 --> 00:40:21,321
There's no place
for Chip and me any more.

551
00:40:24,828 --> 00:40:28,718
You were right, Doctor,
it's time to die.

552
00:40:32,381 --> 00:40:33,905
That's good.

553
00:40:36,977 --> 00:40:38,990
Come on.
There's one last thing I can do.

554
00:40:49,723 --> 00:40:52,477
For Bodeley's sake,
don't do that. He'll be livid.

555
00:40:52,517 --> 00:40:57,311
Oh no, don't! Stop it!
GIGGLES

556
00:40:57,351 --> 00:40:59,468
That's simply not true. Tiny!

557
00:40:59,508 --> 00:41:02,143
Egypt was so dismal.

558
00:41:02,183 --> 00:41:04,301
And the mosquitoes,
I can't tell you. . . . !

559
00:41:04,341 --> 00:41:09,657
Thank you. Just go -
and don't look back.

560
00:41:09,697 --> 00:41:11,181
Good luck.

561
00:41:20,764 --> 00:41:22,401
. .And if you actually see them,
you're shocked.

562
00:41:22,441 --> 00:41:25,529
But don't quote me on that.

563
00:41:25,569 --> 00:41:27,275
Oh, you naughty people! A bientot.

564
00:41:27,315 --> 00:41:28,915
Excuse me, the Lady Cassandra?

565
00:41:28,955 --> 00:41:32,912
Sorry, I don't need anything
right now, I'm fine, thank you.

566
00:41:32,952 --> 00:41:35,778
No, I just wanted to say.
You look beautiful.

567
00:41:36,944 --> 00:41:41,378
Well, that's very kind,
you strange little thing.

568
00:41:41,418 --> 00:41:44,528
Thank you very much. I mean it.

569
00:41:49,539 --> 00:41:52,485
You look. . .

570
00:41:52,525 --> 00:41:53,963
so beautiful.

571
00:41:58,519 --> 00:42:00,077
Thank you.

572
00:42:03,632 --> 00:42:07,311
Oh, my Lord! Are you all right?
What is it, what's wrong?

573
00:42:07,351 --> 00:42:10,465
Someone get some help.
Call a medic or something,

574
00:42:10,505 --> 00:42:13,949
quickly! Who is he?
I don't know, he just came up to me.

575
00:42:13,989 --> 00:42:16,736
Don't even know his name.
He just collapsed.

576
00:42:16,776 --> 00:42:20,142
I think he's dying!
Someone do something.

577
00:42:20,182 --> 00:42:22,689
I've got you, sweetheart.
It's all right.

578
00:42:22,729 --> 00:42:25,895
There you are. There you are. I've
got you.

579
00:42:25,935 --> 00:42:30,354
It'll be all right. There, there.
You poor little thing.

580
00:42:43,585 --> 00:42:47,065
Might I introduce
Her Majesty, Queen Victoria?

581
00:42:53,176 --> 00:42:55,580
Every full moon the howling
rings through the valley.

582
00:42:55,620 --> 00:42:57,967
This is a man who becomes an animal.

583
00:42:58,007 --> 00:43:00,967
A werewolf?
It can't be an actual wolf.

584
00:43:01,007 --> 00:43:02,445
GROWLS

585
00:43:08,447 --> 00:43:09,527
THERE!

586
00:43:09,567 --> 00:43:11,858
Bullets can't stop it.

587
00:43:23,143 --> 00:43:58,976
